Phase 0: Setting up my home lab

Date: 17 November 2026

What I did today
Installed VirtualBox on my Mac
Downloaded Kali Linux and opened it in VirtualBox
Gave Kali 3 GB of RAM and 2 CPUs
Kali is running
New words I learned
Virtual machine (VM): a computer running inside my computer, like an app.
VirtualBox: the free app that runs VMs.
Host: my real computer (my Mac).
Guest: the computer inside VirtualBox (Kali).
Kali Linux: a version of Linux that comes with hacking and security tools.

Why a home lab?

I can practise attacks on my own machines. It's safe and legal, and if I break something I can just delete the VM and start again.

Problems I faced
The newest VirtualBox (7.2) doesn't fully support older Intel Macs like mine, so I used version 7.1.
macOS couldn't open the Kali download (.7z file), so I used an app called The Unarchiver.

